WEBVTT

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:06.720
Shaking my hands 'cuz I'm here for you.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:10.050
Please hug me as tight as you can right now!

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:13.260
Hold on tight to the warmth

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:19.790
that's sprouted inside my little heart.

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:30.040
Never say "It's hopeless" and get down in the dumps!

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:31.470
Go! Go!

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:36.850
Hold on till blue skies spread inside your heart.

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:39.750
Always in the rainy days in my life!

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:43.120
Always in the good days in my life!

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:50.120
Never hesitate! Give all you've got! Never give up!

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:54.500
Shaking my hands 'cuz I'm here for you!

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:57.940
Jumping as high as I can 'cuz I long for you!

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:01.070
The scenery reflected in your eyes

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:04.550
is a memory I carry with me.

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:07.910
Feeling my kick though I've sworn to help you,

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:11.280
I make mistakes when maybe I shouldn't.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.680
It may hurt me deep inside my heart,

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:20.590
but with experience the clouds in there will clear away.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:32.730
There's no way I can lose!

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:34.860
Even a professional player is no match

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:37.110
for unbeatable Sho-chan the supercomputer!

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:38.570
Hisha, 2, 7.

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:40.830
30 seconds left.

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:43.950
Right! Sho-chan, what's the next move?!

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:46.210
<i>Thinking... Thinking...</i>

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:50.080
<i>I don't know. I don't know...</i>

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:52.040
What? What?! WHAT?!

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:55.460
That's impossible!

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:58.300
Sho-chan can predict up to 100,000 moves ahead!

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:01.260
And I can predict up to five million moves ahead.

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:04.060
What?

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:05.830
Don't be so shocked.

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:10.650
Every bit of mathematical or physical information known has been input into her brain.

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:13.770
In human terms, she has an IQ of 50,000.

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:18.490
Naturally, I can predict human behavior patterns as well.

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:19.610
In the case of Kazuya Saotome,

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:23.370
I can predict his patterns up to 30,000 moves ahead.

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:26.320
<i>You've got mail!</i>

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:29.120
Oh! So, you mean...

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:32.220
Yes. The plan has already begun.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:36.370
Kei?

00:02:36.970 --> 00:02:38.490
<i>How do you do?</i>

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:46.010
<i>I saw the report you wrote on your Project Doraemon on the Ochanomizu home page.</i>

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:50.470
<i>I found it very interesting and was moved when reading it.</i>

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:55.440
<i>If you don't mind, I was hoping you'd tell me more.</i>

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:58.610
Moved... Wow, she was moved!

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:05.080
<i>Yamazaki!</i>

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:06.330
<i>Mika!</i>

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:10.920
To be continued.

00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:15.500
Oh, that's so great! "The Whirlwind of Love..."

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:18.840
I want to feel a burning love like that, too!

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:21.340
I'm not really sure I understand it.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:24.350
Maybe it's still too soon for someone as young as you, May.

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:27.560
You understand it, Rena? Wow!

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:34.810
What's that?

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:37.570
Kazuya made it for me.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:40.540
I'm home!

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:41.690
Welcome home, Kazuya!

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:43.240
Welcome home...

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:47.540
Thanks, I could use a drink. It's incredibly hot outside.

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:49.080
Down the hatch!

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:53.600
Great stuff!

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:56.040
No fair!

00:03:57.010 --> 00:03:59.300
That! I want one, too!

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:02.130
I want one! I want one! I want one! I want one! I want one!

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:03.590
All right! All right!

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:06.720
Really? You'll make something for me?!

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:08.700
Well, I'd better go.

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:13.350
Kasumi'll get mad if I stay here too late.

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:14.690
Ikariya, bye-bye!

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:17.020
Buh-ban! Buh-ban! Buh-ban!

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:18.230
Brush your teeth!

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:20.400
See you tomorrow!

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:26.990
Well, we'd better have dinner, too.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:31.290
So, you're going to meet this person?

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:35.790
Yeah. I e-mailed her back, and she wants to meet me tomorrow.

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:38.670
So, this person... is a woman, right?

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:39.810
Yeah.

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:44.010
I see...

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:46.140
N-No, it's not like that!

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:48.550
She's just researching robots, too,

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:52.980
and thought we should share our data!

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:54.670
That's all it is!

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:56.800
Oh, I see.

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:00.400
Kazuya, here. Right here.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:02.710
Oh? What's up?

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:15.660
Sorry. I've never met this person,

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.420
so I can't take you with me.

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:19.630
No problem. I'll watch the apartment.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:22.170
I'll come back as soon as I can.

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:24.840
Hello?

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:26.880
Yo! Am I popular or what?

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:29.350
Nanbara...

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:32.850
What? Is that any way to answer your very best friend!

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:34.610
Two bowls of ramen, please!

00:05:34.610 --> 00:05:35.270
Gotcha!

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:36.850
<i>So, what can I do for you?</i>

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:38.480
Listen up, Saotome!

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:41.570
I'm coming over to your apartment to visit,

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:43.110
so you'd better appreciate it!

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:46.320
You're coming to visit? I'm kinda busy today...

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:50.490
You're what?! Don't you care about your best friend?!

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:52.910
Uh, when are you coming?

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:54.950
Coming? Come and go. Gigolo!

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:57.000
I crack myself up!

00:05:57.000 --> 00:06:01.540
Don't you worry one bit! Time revolves around Kotaro Nanbara!

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:04.260
<i>You just wait there for me. See ya!</i>

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:06.010
Hey!

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:09.730
Oh, man. I don't know when he'll come over.

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:12.770
He's hard for me to deal with.

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:16.770
Now he'll bring the mini-bot along, right?

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:19.560
We'd never get her if she was alone watching the place.

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:22.310
Yeah. Too many obstacles there.

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:24.780
Huh? No one's home...

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:29.700
Anyway, it looks like she's predicted
Saotome's behavior pattern perfectly.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:31.530
Way to go, Cyber Doll Kei!

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:33.780
Okay, there we go! Two bowls of ramen!

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:35.040
Ah! They're here!

00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:43.040
How do you do? I sent you that e-mail yesterday.

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:44.550
My name's Kei.

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:55.310
My... This is your research prototype, isn't it?

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:58.430
I'm Ikariya! Yo!

00:06:58.430 --> 00:06:59.690
Oh, he's adorable!

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:01.150
And so are you.

00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:04.200
According to your report,

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:08.270
the hard drive you put in your robot has
intentionally redundant blank areas on it?

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:11.240
And your theory is that, because of this,

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:13.240
the robot is encouraged to create new programs on its own.

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:14.410
Y-Yeah.

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:16.610
That's incredible!

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:22.670
Oh, this is nasty!

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:26.840
She's going full-force for Saotome's sister-complex.

00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:30.090
She'll be in complete control soon.

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:34.470
I see. You have a good grounding in photonics as well.

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:38.680
And you've applied the Ashura Theory and Brocken's Equation as well! Impressive!

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:40.660
Gee, you shouldn't...

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:48.690
OWWW!

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:49.880
Is anything wrong?

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:55.720
Ow! Kazuya, you stepped on my foot under the table!

00:08:00.890 --> 00:08:02.460
Will you explain to me, please?

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:04.850
That.

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:10.890
Wow. I had no idea this place existed.

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:14.580
Anyway, I basically understand your circumstances now.

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:17.670
I really appreciate what you did before.

00:08:17.670 --> 00:08:17.680
Thank you very much.
I really appreciate what you did before.

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:19.100
Thank you very much.

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:21.100
Oh, that's all right.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:23.600
Still, that's an incredible robot.

00:08:24.010 --> 00:08:27.510
Having her will mean your project should go much smoother, doesn't it?

00:08:27.510 --> 00:08:28.600
Kei!

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:32.280
May isn't like that. She's different.

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:36.780
To me, she's not a robot, but more of a...

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:41.910
Oh, Kazuya!

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:43.540
I'm <i>really</i> sorry about that.

00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:49.290
Kazuya, shall I guess what you want to eat?

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:51.010
Uh, sure.

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:53.510
Simple! Eel kabayaki!

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:55.130
Bingo!

00:08:55.130 --> 00:08:57.260
May, how do you know that?

00:08:57.750 --> 00:08:59.550
It was easy!

00:08:59.550 --> 00:09:02.520
Because, when we passed an eel stand before,

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:04.800
his nose started sniffing like crazy!

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:08.190
Oh, you noticed that, huh?

00:09:09.270 --> 00:09:11.520
I know other things, too!

00:09:13.460 --> 00:09:15.030
What is she waiting for?!

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:17.780
Hurry up and use that sister-con power to take control of him!

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:21.630
And then we'll recover the mini-bot when she does!

00:09:22.770 --> 00:09:23.830
Cheesy plan, huh?

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:26.020
We developed it around your style.

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:28.580
Tulips! The color green!

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:29.710
The smell of erasers! The smell of solder.

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:33.920
Those are all my favorite things. How do you know that?

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:37.680
Because, Kazuya, when you pass by the florist shop,

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:39.910
you always stop to look at the tulips.

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:41.680
Hey, now that you mention it...

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:43.850
And then there's the color green.

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:47.480
For some reason, you always choose green-colored stuff,

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:49.480
like your notebook and other little things.

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:50.690
Oh, jeez...

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:54.110
Forgive me for interrupting, but I'm thirsty.

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:56.740
Could you go buy me something to drink?

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:58.070
Oh, sure thing.

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:00.570
All right! Here's our chance!

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:02.530
We'll grab the mini-bot right now!

00:10:02.680 --> 00:10:04.270
Let's go, Sara!

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:09.290
I'm sorry, May, but can you and Kazuya go back without me?

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:11.480
Huh? Sure.

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:16.340
What's going on? You came up with this plan yourself.

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:18.550
Something strange is going on.

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:23.260
Cyber Doll May has a complete understanding of Kazuya Saotome.

00:10:23.270 --> 00:10:25.810
And she knows him as though she could read his mind.

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:28.680
No maid-type cyber doll is programmed for that.

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:31.400
None of that matters!

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:34.110
The objective is to recover the mini-bot!

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:37.600
Is this anyway for a perfect strategist like you to behave?!

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:44.160
Hello? Anybody home? Hello?

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:46.160
She's processing.

00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:53.370
I'm afraid this is beyond my processing abilities with the available data.

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:56.130
And so, as usual, you want to investigate this further?

00:10:56.570 --> 00:11:00.130
Yes. Something's happening to Cyber Doll May.

00:11:00.440 --> 00:11:03.640
Please, give me two days. I promise I'll recover her then.

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:07.140
No way! Sara, tell her no way!

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:11.150
If that's what you've calculated, then we have no choice.

00:11:12.110 --> 00:11:15.980
All right, you have two days. Then you have to recover her.

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:16.770
Right!

00:11:17.890 --> 00:11:20.650
Spoiling! Coddling! IRRITATING!

00:11:25.230 --> 00:11:26.730
Hello there.

00:11:26.730 --> 00:11:26.740
Thank you for being such a help to Kazuya.
Hello there.

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:29.710
Thank you for being such a help to Kazuya.

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:32.030
Oh, it's no trouble.

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:36.710
Who was that?!

00:11:37.310 --> 00:11:39.800
I wanted more detailed data, so I came over.

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:41.220
Was that any trouble for you?

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:42.810
N-No!

00:11:43.450 --> 00:11:44.840
Oh!

00:11:50.120 --> 00:11:54.770
What's the plus/minus error range if you use this formula?

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:57.360
U-Um, well, if I remember it right, it's...

00:11:57.360 --> 00:12:02.240
I estimate it to be around 0.001.

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:04.110
Huh? Uh, yeah.

00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:05.620
Well?

00:12:10.710 --> 00:12:13.330
Sorry. I tripped.

00:12:17.410 --> 00:12:19.000
Yo!

00:12:23.490 --> 00:12:27.140
<i>That annoying girl's behavior I can understand.</i>

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:28.940
<i>But a cyber doll purposely doing that?</i>

00:12:28.940 --> 00:12:30.320
<i>Why?</i>

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:36.930
Thanks for coming with me.

00:12:36.930 --> 00:12:36.940
Now then, Kazuya...
Thanks for coming with me.

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:39.090
Now then, Kazuya...

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:47.120
Oh, hi, May. Where's Kazuya?

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:49.370
He went off with Kei.

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:50.500
What?!

00:12:52.550 --> 00:12:54.540
She's sure taking her job seriously, I see.

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:57.210
Where's that pretty tutor of yours?

00:12:58.040 --> 00:13:00.450
You've fallen for her, haven't you?!

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:05.430
Oh, boy...

00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:18.260
<i>Why is it? Why?</i>

00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:33.550
<i>I want to be bigger.</i>

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:38.990
Huh? Where's my mirror?

00:13:41.660 --> 00:13:44.380
And my lipstick, too. Well, then...

00:13:44.730 --> 00:13:46.260
Rena!

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:47.630
Don't lie to me!

00:13:48.740 --> 00:13:51.140
I'm headed over to Professor Yumi's place.

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:53.680
I'll be back by nightfall.

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:54.980
See you later.

00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:11.700
Whatcha doing?

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:14.870
You've got ketchup all over your face!

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:16.560
No, it's not!

00:14:21.940 --> 00:14:25.710
As promised, you have a full day today.

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:28.680
I understand. Both of you, please come this way.

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:31.260
Oh? You got a surprise for us in here?

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:33.880
Maybe some ramen for us?

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:36.600
<i>Hey! What's the big idea?!</i>

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:38.060
<i>Is this a double-cross?!</i>

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:40.060
You two would just get in the way.

00:14:40.060 --> 00:14:42.190
Just wait there and be quiet please.

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:43.690
Sara, bust that door down!

00:14:46.060 --> 00:14:50.950
I reinforced the door with 31 mm of iron plate yesterday.

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:52.530
See you.

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:55.120
Sara! What's your strength limit?

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:57.250
30 millimeters of iron plate.

00:14:57.250 --> 00:15:00.210
Oh, one lousy millimeter!

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:02.540
Well played, Cyber Doll Kei.

00:15:02.810 --> 00:15:04.170
<i>Yamazaki!</i>

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:05.590
<i>Mika!</i>

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:13.800
Why do you just keep sighing like that?

00:15:13.820 --> 00:15:15.760
Oh? Am I?

00:15:17.030 --> 00:15:18.560
There you go again!

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:20.810
You're like some lovesick schoolgirl!

00:15:21.830 --> 00:15:24.270
I'll bet this is your first crush, too.

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:28.280
E-Even if you say that, I don't know anything about love!

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:30.030
I was kidding!

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:35.620
Hey, doesn't Yamazaki look like someone we know?

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:37.080
It's Kazuya!

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:38.910
Doesn't look like him! Doesn't look like him!

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:44.250
<i>Having met, then parted, they meet again.</i>

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:49.320
<i>The winds of love blow between them, reunited at last.</i>

00:15:55.460 --> 00:15:57.680
N-No...

00:15:58.430 --> 00:16:00.560
Hello?

00:16:07.010 --> 00:16:09.610
Trouble! Kasumi!

00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:13.200
What's wrong? Why were you crying?

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:14.870
I don't know.

00:16:15.550 --> 00:16:17.790
<i>This is unprecedented.</i>

00:16:18.350 --> 00:16:21.410
<i>Maid-type cyber dolls aren't programmed to cry.</i>

00:16:24.390 --> 00:16:26.380
May disappeared with Kei?

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:29.380
Yeah. While I was looking for Kasumi.

00:16:32.570 --> 00:16:33.720
Kazuya!

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:36.680
You can examine my body if you want, but...

00:16:36.680 --> 00:16:40.220
Don't worry. I'll keep my promise.

00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:45.440
I just want to know about your programming.

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:47.440
Well, if it's just that...

00:16:47.780 --> 00:16:50.860
Although I think Kazuya wants to know about it, too.

00:16:53.120 --> 00:16:56.450
That's why I asked him last evening.

00:16:57.030 --> 00:16:59.950
About the two of us researching this together.

00:17:00.400 --> 00:17:04.250
No way. I could never look into May's programming.

00:17:04.250 --> 00:17:07.210
Strange. even though he's interested in it.

00:17:07.210 --> 00:17:09.750
I am, but...

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:13.720
If I were May, I wouldn't want someone peeking into my heart.

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:16.220
That's why I don't want to do that to her.

00:17:18.650 --> 00:17:21.470
<i>So, that's what you said, Kazuya.</i>

00:17:23.320 --> 00:17:24.970
Okay, lie down.

00:17:25.920 --> 00:17:26.980
Look...

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:31.480
I know. I'll never bother Kazuya again.

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:46.160
May!

00:17:47.880 --> 00:17:49.750
Please don't look, Kazuya!

00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:53.420
You're too late. I just finished.

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:56.800
Kei, you said you wouldn't do this!

00:17:56.800 --> 00:18:00.800
Thank you, Kazuya. But it's okay.

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:05.270
I only have part of her MAID program loaded in here.

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:07.270
MAID program?

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:12.270
We cyber dolls function using the MAID program.

00:18:12.270 --> 00:18:13.280
"We"?

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:16.320
Yes. I'm a cyber doll as well.

00:18:17.510 --> 00:18:19.780
It's no use. I can't analyze it.

00:18:26.280 --> 00:18:28.040
Kei, what are you doing?!

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:32.320
I'm assimilating part of May's system for analysis.

00:18:38.660 --> 00:18:40.470
Kei!

00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:43.470
Impossible! A rejection?

00:18:43.870 --> 00:18:46.630
The program I've assimilated is rejecting me!

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:48.230
Kei, stop it!

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:49.640
Stop it, please!

00:18:49.640 --> 00:18:52.520
A little more. A little more, and I can analyze it!

00:18:53.580 --> 00:18:55.730
No, it's evolving.

00:18:55.730 --> 00:18:59.240
The program's growing!

00:19:01.050 --> 00:19:02.410
Kei!

00:19:06.690 --> 00:19:17.340
Kazuya!

00:19:18.870 --> 00:19:19.880
Are you okay?

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:23.010
So... So, that's what it is.

00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:26.680
That's what's causing May's strange behavior.

00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:28.290
Strange behavior?

00:19:31.580 --> 00:19:34.560
May I ask you one question?

00:19:34.560 --> 00:19:36.070
Sure.

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:38.400
Why did you help me?

00:19:38.400 --> 00:19:41.570
Huh? I'm not sure I can explain why.

00:19:43.930 --> 00:19:46.370
Tell me why! Why did you?!

00:19:46.370 --> 00:19:49.580
Let's see! Just because, I guess.

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:04.780
<i>You've got mail!</i>

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:08.010
<i>I truly appreciate all you've done.</i>

00:20:08.010 --> 00:20:10.310
<i>I'm going on a journey.</i>

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:12.280
<i>Farewell. Kei.</i>

00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:15.610
Damn you, Kei!

00:20:15.610 --> 00:20:17.020
Unforgivable!

00:20:18.190 --> 00:20:23.290
<i>And so, like she promised, Kei left us.</i>

00:20:25.030 --> 00:20:27.530
Well, I'm back!

00:20:28.770 --> 00:20:30.250
You said you were going on a journey!

00:20:31.310 --> 00:20:33.620
Well, for some reason, I wound up back here!

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:35.250
I have to find out the cause of all this.

00:20:35.250 --> 00:20:37.750
Kei, this isn't what you promised!

00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:39.000
Yo...

00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:44.760
I'll be staying here, starting today.

00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:46.010
How do you do?

00:20:46.010 --> 00:20:48.220
What does she mean, she's staying here?!

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:51.930
<i>Kei's face is bright red, Kasumi's in a really bad mood,</i>

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:53.810
<i>and Kazuya is just cowering.</i>

00:20:54.460 --> 00:20:57.310
<i>How can this get any worse?</i>

00:20:58.330 --> 00:20:59.360
Coming!

00:21:03.640 --> 00:21:07.030
I'm a representative from the Cyberdyne Corporation.

00:21:07.030 --> 00:21:08.410
My name is Sara.

00:21:09.210 --> 00:21:10.510
Aren't you the girl who...?

00:21:10.510 --> 00:21:12.040
Mr. Kazuya Saotome,

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:16.610
I'm reclaiming the Cyber Doll May unit which you ordered.

00:21:18.490 --> 00:21:20.840
As you have not paid for her,

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:23.720
my company is now forced to cancel your license agreement.

00:21:24.190 --> 00:21:27.750
Reclamation well be carried out tomorrow at 6:00 PM.

00:21:37.010 --> 00:21:46.040
Kimi no mae de mimi made akaku naru no wa

00:21:46.040 --> 00:21:50.320
Doushite darou

00:21:50.320 --> 00:21:56.520
Futari-kiri wa nigatedashi

00:21:56.520 --> 00:22:03.690
Oshaberi mo gikochinai

00:22:04.430 --> 00:22:11.500
Okashii yo ne ishiki shisugi

00:22:11.500 --> 00:22:20.640
Kore ga koi na no? sonna no zettai mitomenai

00:22:21.050 --> 00:22:27.650
Sunao ni narenai sunao ni naritai

00:22:27.650 --> 00:22:34.320
Hontou no kimochi wa kokoro no naka

00:22:34.320 --> 00:22:41.930
Itsuka kimi ga oshiete

00:22:44.710 --> 00:22:46.260
For 19 years I've lived as his rival,

00:22:46.260 --> 00:22:47.630
all to hear Saotome scream in anguish!

00:22:47.630 --> 00:22:49.700
And with that moment at hand,

00:22:49.700 --> 00:22:52.290
my heart is filled with passion! Action! Formation!

00:22:52.290 --> 00:22:53.810
Uh, Sara? What are you doing?

00:22:53.810 --> 00:22:55.720
I'm going home.

00:22:55.720 --> 00:22:56.390
Huh? No way.

00:22:56.390 --> 00:22:57.100
Yes way.

00:22:57.100 --> 00:22:59.250
"Until Today, I've Really..."
